      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:1:87:5",
      "text": [
        " مَنْ كَسَا مُؤْمِناً ثَوْباً مِنْ عُرْيٍ كَسَاهُ اللَّهُ مِنْ إِسْتَبْرَقِ الْجَنَّةِ وَ مَنْ كَسَا مُؤْمِناً ثَوْباً مِنْ غِنًى لَمْ يَزَلْ فِي سِتْرٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ مَا بَقِيَ مِنَ الثَّوْبِ خِرْقَةٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Khalid, from Usman Bin Isa, from bdullah Bin Sinan, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, that he<sup>asws</sup> used to say: ‘The one who clothes a <span class=\"iTxt\">Momin</span> with a cloth from bareness, Allah<sup>azwj</sup> would Clothe him from the brocades of the Paradise; and the one who clothes a <span class=\"iTxt\">Momin</span> with a cloth from adequacy, would not cease to be in a Veil from Allah<sup>azwj</sup> for as long as there remains a rag from the cloth’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. A number of our people have narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Khalid from ‘Uthman ibn ‘Isa from ‘Abd Allah ibn Sinan from abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) who has said the following: “Whoever provides clothes for a believer (while in need) for covering, Allah will dress up the former with Istabraq (a kind of fine clothing) of paradise. Whoever provides clothes for a believer (while he already has enough) for covering he will live under the protection of Allah as long as anything is left of that clothing.” "
        ]
      }
    },
